Article 2 (Duties) The Armed Forces Chemical, Biological and Radiological Defense Command (hereinafter referred to as the "Command") shall perform the following duties:
1. Matters concerning CBR defense operations by the armed forces and CBR defense operations for the public and support therefor (support shall be provided in cooperation with the relevant agencies and military services);
2. Matters concerning support for countermeasures against CBR terrorism (support shall be provided in cooperation with the relevant agencies and military services);
3. Matters concerning the armed forces' analysis of environmental pollution and verification of radiological safety;
4. Matters concerning support for responding to CBR incidents and disasters;
5. Matters concerning performance improvement, testing, and verification of CBR defense equipment and materiel;
6. Matters concerning verification, analysis, copying, and disposal support for CBR weapons;
7. Matters concerning development of a joint CBR defense education and training system.
